[66.830216, "o", "usage: gpu [-h] [--key KEY] [--timeout TIMEOUT] [--cwd CWD] [--detach] [--config CONFIG] {policy,run,stop,exec,status,wait,push,pull,refresh,sync} [args ...]\r\n\r\nGPU boxes through a shared Modal service\r\n\r\npositional arguments:\r\n  {policy,run,stop,exec,status,wait,push,pull,refresh,sync}\r\n  args\r\n\r\noptions:\r\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\r\n  --key KEY             Reuse this request ID after a lost response\r\n  --timeout TIMEOUT     Optional timeout for the remote command, in seconds\r\n  --cwd CWD\r\n  --detach\r\n  --config CONFIG       Optional JSON config instead of environment configuration\r\n\r\nCommands:\r\n  gpu policy\r\n  gpu run [options] -- PROGRAM [ARG ...]\r\n  gpu stop BOX\r\n  gpu exec BOX [options] -- PROGRAM [ARG ...]\r\n  gpu status COMMAND\r\n  gpu wait COMMAND\r\n  gpu push BOX LOCAL REMOTE\r\n  gpu pull BOX REMOTE LOCAL\r\n  gpu refresh BOX\r\n  gpu sync\r\n\r\nrun starts a GPU box with its first command and returns command and box IDs.\r\nThe run command is the sandbox entrypoint; when it exits, the"]
[66.830263, "o", " box stops.\r\nexec is available while that box is running.\r\nrun and exec wait unless --detach is set.\r\nstatus and wait take the command IDs they return.\r\nThe -- separator starts the remote program and its arguments.\r\n"]
